target: internal/record/record.go
verify: go test ./internal/record/ -count=1 -run 'TestConvergenceRules'
expect: a_cycle_with_no_agents_field_spends_nothing
why:    an absent `agents` must contribute 0 to the spend sum, matching the Python's `or 0`. A mutant contributing 1 instead survived every case in a differential run during review (its 18,041-store count is the review's and is not reproducible from this repo), because catching it needs a cap small enough for one agent to cross it and no fixture had one. Not writer-reachable (`--agents` is required=True) and absent from all 59 real cycle rows, so this pins a parity claim that would otherwise stand with nothing behind it.
--- old
		if c.Agents != nil {
			spent += *c.Agents // absent reads as zero here, matching the Python's `or 0`
		}
--- new
		if c.Agents == nil {
			spent += 1
		} else {
			spent += *c.Agents
		}
